WebSocket is basically an application protocol  which makes use of TCP as transport layer.

WebSocket is duplex connection over tcp.

tcp - statefull[store meta data on both client and server], http- stateless [we underneath uses tcp]

An API gateway handles authentication and security policies, while a load balancer API distributes network traffic across multiple servers.

 In that case, an API gateway could provide a single entry point for all these services.

A load balancer is a service that distributes incoming traffic across multiple servers or resources.


Just as HTTP, the WebSocket protocol operates on the top of the TCP connection. However, while the HTTP protocol is strictly unidirectional, which causes critical limitations to the communication process, WebSocket is a bidirectional protocol that enables full-duplex communication.


HEAD, OPTIONS, GET, PUT, TRACE, and DELETE are idempotent

you should always place the load balancer behind your network firewall to protect your business-critical systems.



