pub sub - https://chatgpt.com/c/68a76672-2f00-8327-9d73-d316f6cc1e69
🔹 1. RabbitMQ

Queue (P2P) → Work Queue

Producer → Queue → Multiple Consumers

Each message is delivered to only one consumer.

Pub/Sub → Fanout Exchange

Producer → Exchange → Multiple Queues (one per subscriber)

Each subscriber gets its own copy of the message.

🔹 4. Apache Kafka

Queue (P2P) → Consumer Group

Multiple consumers in the same group.

Each partition is assigned to only one consumer in that group.

Messages are split between them (load balancing).

Pub/Sub → Multiple Consumer Groups

Each consumer group gets its own full copy of the data.

One producer can fan out events to many services (each in its own group).